<title>USA: Sri Lanka buys Canadian and Australian wheat-trade.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka buys Canadian and Australian wheat-trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka bought on Thursday night a total of 100,000 tonnes wheat in two positions -- one 50,000-tonne lot of Canadian wheat and one 50,000-tonne lot of Australian wheat, U.S. exporters said.  </p>
<p>The Australian hard wheat was sold at $191.95 a tonne, Cost and Freight slated for May 27-June 5 shipment, one U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>The Canadian western red spring wheat was sold at $189.42, C &amp; F, a Canadian Pacific port, set for June 16-25 shipment, the exporter added.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
</text>
